  "content": {
    "id": "p21-question-60-67-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $x=\\ln(a)$, $y=\\ln(b)$ and $z=\\ln(c)$. Express the following in terms of $x$, $y$, $z$, and constants.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\ln(abc)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x+y+z$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\ln(abc)&=\\ln(a)+\\ln(b)+\\ln(c)\\\\\\ln(abc)&=x+y+z\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(\\ln(ab))^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+y)^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\ln(ab))^2&=(\\ln(a)+\\ln(b))^2\\\\(\\ln(ab))^2&=(x+y)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{a^2}{bc}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x-y-z$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\ln\\left(\\frac{a^2}{bc}\\right)&=2\\ln(a)-\\ln(b)-\\ln(c)\\\\\\ln\\left(\\frac{a^2}{bc}\\right)&=2x-y-z\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{ab^2}}{2c}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{x}{2}+y-z-\\ln(2)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{ab^2}}{2c}\\right)&=\\frac12\\ln(ab^2)-\\ln(2)-\\ln(c)\\\\\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{ab^2}}{2c}\\right)&=\\frac12\\ln(a)+\\ln(b)-\\ln(2)-\\ln(c)\\\\\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{ab^2}}{2c}\\right)&=\\frac{x}{2}+y-z-\\ln(2)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\log_b(a)+\\log_c(a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{x}{y}+\\dfrac{x}{z}$, where $y\\ne0$ and $z\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_b(a)+\\log_c(a)&=\\frac{\\ln(a)}{\\ln(b)}+\\frac{\\ln(a)}{\\ln(c)}\\\\\\log_b(a)+\\log_c(a)&=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{x}{z}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe bases require $b,c\\ne1$, so $y,z\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\ln(ab)\\,\\ln(bc)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+y)(y+z)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\ln(ab)\\,\\ln(bc)&=(\\ln(a)+\\ln(b))(\\ln(b)+\\ln(c))\\\\\\ln(ab)\\,\\ln(bc)&=(x+y)(y+z)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\ln(ab)}{\\ln(bc)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{x+y}{y+z}$, where $y+z\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\ln(ab)}{\\ln(bc)}&=\\frac{\\ln(a)+\\ln(b)}{\\ln(b)+\\ln(c)}\\\\\\frac{\\ln(ab)}{\\ln(bc)}&=\\frac{x+y}{y+z}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe denominator requires $bc\\ne1$, so $y+z\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-question-60-67-part-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1+\\log_a(b)}{\\log_b(c)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{xy+y^2}{xz}$, where $x,y,z\\ne0$.\n\nChange both logarithms to base $e$, then simplify the compound fraction.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+\\log_a(b)}{\\log_b(c)}&=\\frac{1+\\frac{y}{x}}{\\frac{z}{y}}\\\\\\frac{1+\\log_a(b)}{\\log_b(c)}&=\\frac{x+y}{x}\\times\\frac{y}{z}\\\\\\frac{1+\\log_a(b)}{\\log_b(c)}&=\\frac{xy+y^2}{xz}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $a,b,c\\ne1$, so $x,y,z\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
